  explanation: "For rand_xorshift 0.5.0, the Aeneas proof establishes the exact try_next_u32 word and state update for every four-u32 state, using three explicit std wrapping-operator models. With t=x XOR (x << 11), r=w XOR (w >> 19) XOR t XOR (t >> 8); the returned value is Ok(r) and state becomes (y,z,w,r), using 32-bit logical operations. A separate Lean theorem derives preservation of a nonzero state from this exact transition. Independently, Kani checks the unchanged from_seed body for every 16-byte seed: four little-endian u32 words are decoded, and the all-zero input is replaced by four 0x0BAD5EED words. The constructed state is nonzero. A second Kani harness checks that the original next_u32 body preserves every nonzero four-word state. These seed and preservation checks are supplementary Kani results, not an Aeneas seed-body claim. No original Rust source or manifest is changed. A further original-source Kani check covers every 16-byte seed, including the zero-seed fallback: from_seed followed by try_next_u64 returns the same little-endian low/high word composition as two try_next_u32 calls on an identical clone, and derived equality confirms every resulting state word agrees. This is a public-API relational guarantee over seed-constructed states, not an independent recurrence specification. Separate Kani also executes the original manual Debug formatter for every public from_seed input or seed_from_u64 input. With default formatting and a fixed64-byte writer it emits exactly \"XorShiftRng {}\" (13bytes), preserves the zero suffix and correct length; a writer rejecting the first write instead propagates fmt::Error with no bytes retained. A separate original try_fill_bytes relation is checked for every16-byte seed, every initial8-byte array and every requested prefix length0..8. Filling returns Ok, writes exactly the little-endian prefix from ceil(length/4) actual next32 calls, preserves the unused array suffix and yields an equal complete final generator state." -> "For rand_xorshift 0.5.0, the Aeneas proof establishes the exact try_next_u32 word and state update for every four-u32 state, using three explicit std wrapping-operator models. With t=x XOR (x << 11), r=w XOR (w >> 19) XOR t XOR (t >> 8); the returned value is Ok(r) and state becomes (y,z,w,r), using 32-bit logical operations. A separate Lean theorem derives preservation of a nonzero state from this exact transition. Independently, Kani checks the unchanged from_seed body for every 16-byte seed: four little-endian u32 words are decoded, and the all-zero input is replaced by four 0x0BAD5EED words. The constructed state is nonzero. A second Kani harness checks that the original next_u32 body preserves every nonzero four-word state. These seed and preservation checks are supplementary Kani results, not an Aeneas seed-body claim. No original Rust source or manifest is changed. A further original-source Kani check covers every 16-byte seed, including the zero-seed fallback: from_seed followed by try_next_u64 returns the same little-endian low/high word composition as two try_next_u32 calls on an identical clone, and derived equality confirms every resulting state word agrees. This is a public-API relational guarantee over seed-constructed states, not an independent recurrence specification. Separate Kani also executes the original manual Debug formatter for every public from_seed input or seed_from_u64 input. With default formatting and a fixed64-byte writer it emits exactly \"XorShiftRng {}\" (13bytes), preserves the zero suffix and correct length; a writer rejecting the first write instead propagates fmt::Error with no bytes retained. A separate original try_fill_bytes relation is checked for every16-byte seed, every initial8-byte array and every requested prefix length0..8. Filling returns Ok, writes exactly the little-endian prefix from ceil(length/4) actual next32 calls, preserves the unused array suffix and yields an equal complete final generator state. Separate original from_rng/try_from_rng Kani relations cover concrete source protocols: every nonzero16-byte seed, optionally preceded by one all-zero block, produces the same complete state as public from_seed after exactly1or2 source fills. Fallible sources additionally propagate every u32 error payload after zero or one discarded zero block, preserving the expected call count even if the failing fill first writes arbitrary bytes."
  environment: "Original crates.io rand_xorshift 0.5.0; Rust nightly-2026-09-17; Charon 08d7c9d50144bd84848212c24701253585e90d1f; official Aeneas frontend/library be86ab0f1989d04944292b345b24c435be3ad10a; Lean 4.35.0. Official start-from and split-files options select the original body and three external operators. Kani 0.68.0 / CBMC 6.11.0 / Rust nightly-2026-08-21 provide the supplementary checks detailed below. The Lean theorem audit allows only propext, Classical.choice, and Quot.sound. cargo-proofs 0.4.1 uses the documented CA-trust, upstream audit-variable, and exact rand_core::TryRng catalogue-alias compatibility fixes without changing the allowed-axiom policy. Supplementary seed/nonzero Kani run: 2 harnesses, 327 checks, zero failures (237 seed plus 90 preservation), with unwind 20 and unwinding assertions enabled. All 128 seed bits and all nonzero four-word states are quantified. Nonzero.lean is independently built/audited with only the standard three axioms; it is supplementary to the unchanged single machine API mapping. See SEED-VERIFICATION.md and evidence/kani-seed for exact source-prefix hashes and verification-module provenance. Additional public composition supplement: ordinary Kani harness,294 checks/0fail/5unreachable, original11 archive files and actual rand_core0.10.0 19files authenticated, no observer/model; evidence/kani-public-composition. Additional original Debug Kani supplement:2217checks/0fail/133unreachable, default/core0.10.0/nightly2026-08-21; evidence/kani-debug. Ordinary Kani supplement; the single Aeneas mapping is unchanged. Further original fill8 Kani supplement:379checks/0fail/5unreachable, unwind20, default/rand_core0.10.0/nightly2026-08-21; evidence/kani-fill8. Aeneascount1 remains unchanged." -> "Original crates.io rand_xorshift 0.5.0; Rust nightly-2026-09-17; Charon 08d7c9d50144bd84848212c24701253585e90d1f; official Aeneas frontend/library be86ab0f1989d04944292b345b24c435be3ad10a; Lean 4.35.0. Official start-from and split-fi