  limitations: "The single Aeneas API mapping remains try_next_u32 on x86_64 without serde. from_seed and original nonzero-state preservation are independent Kani body checks. Aeneas extraction of the original seed body remains blocked by mutable zip iteration. Kani uses Rust nightly-2026-08-21 while Aeneas extraction uses nightly-2026-09-17; these are not mechanically linked proofs of one toolchain's std bodies. The three wrapping models retain their reviewed Rust-to-Lean bridge. The all-zero state is still covered by the exact step theorem; the initial-nonzero guarantee is for from_seed, not every unverified initialization or serialization path. General-state next_u64 correctness, fill_bytes, external-RNG initialization, formatting, inherited Rng wrappers and serde remain unverified. No period, distribution or cryptographic property is established. The separate try_next_u64 composition check covers only states constructed from_seed under default features and rand_core0.10.0. Arbitrary Rust-valid all-zero internal states, serde states, other histories, independent mathematical output formulas and a formal Rust-to-Lean bridge remain outside that check. This Debug result is limited to these public constructor images, default format flags and the fixed accepting-or-first-error writer; arbitrary Formatter states, partial-prefix errors, general writers and arbitrary private states are not established. The fill supplement covers only lengths0..8 in an8-byte allocation and states from public from_seed; arbitrary lengths/allocations, serde and arbitrary private states remain unproved. A separate0..64 attempt timed out and supplies no completed guarantee. This is an original public-API relation, not an independent recurrence proof or Rust-to-Lean equivalence." -> "The single Aeneas API mapping remains try_next_u32 on x86_64 without serde. from_seed and original nonzero-state preservation are independent Kani body checks. Aeneas extraction of the original seed body remains blocked by mutable zip iteration. Kani uses Rust nightly-2026-08-21 while Aeneas extraction uses nightly-2026-09-17; these are not mechanically linked proofs of one toolchain's std bodies. The three wrapping models retain their reviewed Rust-to-Lean bridge. The all-zero state is still covered by the exact step theorem; the initial-nonzero guarantee is for from_seed, not every unverified initialization or serialization path. General-state next_u64 correctness, fill_bytes, external-RNG initialization, formatting, inherited Rng wrappers and serde remain unverified. No period, distribution or cryptographic property is established. The separate try_next_u64 composition check covers only states constructed from_seed under default features and rand_core0.10.0. Arbitrary Rust-valid all-zero internal states, serde states, other histories, independent mathematical output formulas and a formal Rust-to-Lean bridge remain outside that check. This Debug result is limited to these public constructor images, default format flags and the fixed accepting-or-first-error writer; arbitrary Formatter states, partial-prefix errors, general writers and arbitrary private states are not established. The fill supplement covers only lengths0..8 in an8-byte allocation and states from public from_seed; arbitrary lengths/allocations, serde and arbitrary private states remain unproved. A separate0..64 attempt timed out and supplies no completed guarantee. This is an original public-API relation, not an independent recurrence proof or Rust-to-Lean equivalence. Source-based initialization is checked only for these concrete TryRng implementations and zero-or-one preliminary-zero protocol. It does not establish arbitrary source behavior, unbounded zero retries, unconditional termination, generic callback effects or serde behavior. Equality with from_seed is a relational result, not literal delegation or an independent seed-decoding specification."
